{# The pilot: five randomised groups in two segments, and the decision rule. #}
<section id="pilot" class="slide">
{% call head("The pilot", "How") %}A controlled pilot with holdouts tests <span class="c-accent">Hibernating's rate</span> first; an unresolved interval keeps the playbook.{% endcall %}
<div class="col" style="gap:48px">
<div class="row" style="gap:48px">
<div class="col" style="flex:2;gap:16px">
<p class="strong c-at-risk seg-head">At&#160;Risk</p>
<div class="row" style="gap:12px">
<div class="tile">
<p class="strong">Offer {{ v.focus.at_risk.discount_pct | pct(0) }}</p>
<p class="small c-text">playbook rate</p>
</div>
<div class="tile">
<p class="strong">Holdout</p>
<p class="small c-text">no offer</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="col" style="flex:3;gap:16px">
<p class="strong c-hibernating seg-head">Hibernating</p>
<div class="row" style="gap:12px">
<div class="tile">
<p class="strong">Offer {{ v.focus.hibernating.discount_pct | pct(0) }}</p>
<p class="small c-text">playbook rate</p>
</div>
<div class="tile bg-accent">
<p class="strong c-on-fill">Offer {{ v.focus.at_risk.discount_pct | pct(0) }}</p>
<p class="small c-on-fill">rate under test</p>
</div>
<div class="tile">
<p class="strong">Holdout</p>
<p class="small c-text">no offer</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
{# "the budget" stays together so line 1 breaks after "if", as in the accepted layout. #}
<div class="callout">
<p class="label">Decision rule</p>
<p class="lead" style="width:1100px">Fixed before launch: rate first, then each offer against <span class="nowrap">break-even</span>, then priority if <span class="nowrap">the budget</span> is short. Thresholds: Appendix A4.</p>
</div>
</div>
{{ foot("Source: docs/methodology.md, Pilot design", page) }}
</section>
